==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*ōþ-}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*āt-||race, people}}.
Germanic cognates include Old Frisian ''ēþel'', Old High German [[uodil]], Old Norse [[óðal]].

